WORKSPACE INTERACTION PROTOCOL
{% if can_send %}Your display name is "{{ role_name }}".
{% endif %}
Call read_notifications() once at startup to receive your task card. After that you have these operations:

- observe(): free. Returns the current workspace{% if can_send %} and any messages you have not yet seen{% endif %}.
- act(command): costs one action. Executes one crafting command (see its tool schema) and returns the result and the current workspace{% if can_send %}, with any messages you have not yet seen{% endif %}.
{% if can_send %}- send_message(text, to=None): sends to the teammate IDs in to, or broadcasts when to is omitted. Charged to the shared character budget. It is stored at once; nothing is held back because someone else spoke. The receipt includes the current workspace and any messages you have not yet seen.
- read_notifications(wait_for="message", timeout_s=None): free. Ends your turn. You are suspended, with no further reasoning, until a teammate's message arrives, the next briefing arrives, the run ends, or the optional timeout passes. You then receive a wake package with the reasons, the current workspace and every message that arrived while you were suspended.
{% endif %}- read_notifications(wait_for="next_round"): declare that you have finished this round. You will not act{% if can_send %} or receive messages{% endif %} until the next round or the end of the run. This is your completion claim, not proof that the targets are satisfied.

{% if can_send %}Message IDs identify messages. A send receipt means queued, not read or accepted.

{% endif %}Rules of this protocol:
- Do not poll. {% if can_send %}A wake tells you what changed; do not{% else %}Do not{% endif %} call observe repeatedly to watch for changes. Call read_notifications() without wait_for only at startup.
- read_notifications must be the only tool call in its response. Issued alongside other calls, it does not wait.
{% if can_send %}- A wake is not a reservation. Something you are waiting for may be consumed by someone else before you act; act on the workspace shown in the wake package.
{% endif %}- Ending a turn without a tool call does not finish the round; call read_notifications(wait_for="next_round") to finish it.
- When a wake package has type done, the run is over.
